---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Notice from "../components/Notice.astro";
import { site } from "../config";

const description = `How to delete data from ${site.name}. The game has no account. Progress stays on your device.`;
---

<Base title="Your Data" description={description}>
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="kicker">Your Data</p>
    <h1>Your Data</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {site.updated}</p>
    <Notice />
    <p>
      {site.name} does not create an account. There is no login, no profile on a server of ours,
      and no cloud copy of your game.
    </p>

    <h2>What is stored</h2>
    <p>
      The app keeps your progress on the device: levels, scores, energy, shards, cosmetics, and
      settings. The save is stored locally under the name {site.saveKey}. We do not receive it.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, that message is the
      information we hold. We use it to reply and keep it in our email account. You can ask us to
      delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>How to delete it</h2>
    <p>
      On iPhone or iPad, delete {site.name}. The system deletes the app's local data with the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      On Android, clear the app's storage in Settings, or uninstall the app. Either one deletes the
      local save.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no server save for us to erase. After you do this, nothing from the game itself
      remains with us.
    </p>
    <p>
      To ask us to delete an email you sent, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> from that same address and say you want the
      correspondence deleted.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising identifiers</h2>
    <p>
      When ads are enabled, an advertising identifier is handled by your device and by Google
      AdMob. We do not store it as an account. You can reset or delete it in your device settings.
      See the <a href="/advertising">Advertising Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.publisher}<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
